WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.550
- Oh my gosh.
(audience cheering)

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:03.360
- Oh my gosh.
- I miss you.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.680
So, wait, have y'all met before?

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.024
- We've never met, no.
- No, but I'm a big fan.

00:00:07.024 --> 00:00:08.490
- Oh, well thank you, same.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.800
- And I have to say, you
were amazing on "Is It Cake?"

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.838
- Listen, I can nail a cake.

00:00:13.838 --> 00:00:14.671
(audience cheering)
- [Kelly} I can nail it.

00:00:14.671 --> 00:00:15.661
- I can nail a cake.

00:00:15.661 --> 00:00:16.860
- You've got a lot of other skills,

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.076
but you really brought it on "Is It Cake?"

00:00:18.076 --> 00:00:20.550
- (laughing) I appreciate it, thank you.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:22.710
- Wait, Lena just had
her one-year anniversary.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:23.700
You just had your second, right?

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:24.533
- Second, yeah.

00:00:24.533 --> 00:00:26.071
- That's so incredible.
(audience cheering)

00:00:26.071 --> 00:00:27.030
How's it going?

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:28.500
- [Fortune] So far so good.
- [Kelly] Yeah?

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.333
- [Fortune] Yeah.

00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:30.166
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:00:30.166 --> 00:00:31.170
Well, it looks great.

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:32.003
- Look at that, come on.

00:00:32.003 --> 00:00:34.332
- And your wife is a kindergarten teacher.

00:00:34.332 --> 00:00:35.280
- She was for 12 years.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:36.113
She got tired.

00:00:36.113 --> 00:00:37.290
Those kids wore her out.

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:38.250
- [Kelly] Yeah, well
they're kindergartners.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.240
- They are, yeah.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.070
So she's taking a little break.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.510
- So wait, this new comedy special

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:44.490
kind of picks up where the
last one left off, right?

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:46.207
- Yeah, my first hour special,

00:00:46.207 --> 00:00:48.510
"Sweet and Salty" was very much about me.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:49.530
- [Kelly] Love.
- Oh, thank you.

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:50.610
- [Kelly] God, you're so funny.

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.650
- It was about me kind of finding myself,

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:56.130
and that journey of figuring out who I am.

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:58.920
This one is me as an adult, you know,

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.750
getting married, getting engaged,

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:04.290
and also, I'm not what you might think

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:05.460
from what meets the eye.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:06.840
You'll have to watch and see.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:07.673
- Oh, I like it.

00:01:07.673 --> 00:01:08.670
I know the tease was nice.

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:09.694
I saw her go, wait.

00:01:09.694 --> 00:01:10.527
- Oh, that was that a good tease?

00:01:10.527 --> 00:01:11.442
- Yes, it was

00:01:11.442 --> 00:01:13.260
- [Kelly] Her body, her
whole body just shifted.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:14.160
- That's exactly right.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.685
I'm gonna go home tonight
and figure out what you are.

00:01:16.685 --> 00:01:17.760
- Yeah (Kelly and audience laughing).

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.050
Watch that special.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:20.880
- So wait, do you feel like the pandemic

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.050
taught you anything about yourself?

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:23.400
Did anything happen that you use?

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.715
- Well, don't let this
camo jacket fool you.

00:01:25.715 --> 00:01:26.700
(audience laughing)

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:29.550
I found out I have no
survival skills whatsoever.

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:30.383
- Oh really?

00:01:30.383 --> 00:01:31.600
I love stuff like that.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:32.433
- You do?

00:01:32.433 --> 00:01:34.050
- I have so many books.

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:34.980
If I ever die,

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:36.697
people are gonna look
at my library and go,

00:01:36.697 --> 00:01:38.640
"Did she think, like,"

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.830
well, we did have a global pandemic,

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.510
but, "Did she think the
end of times were coming?"

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:43.560
I find it interesting.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:45.000
- I thought, as a lesbian,

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.980
the end of times would be like,

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.062
I would be totally fine with that.

00:01:49.062 --> 00:01:50.010
(audience and Kelly laughing)

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:51.630
- The end of times would be your time.

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:52.620
- It would be my time.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:55.123
Put me in a bunker with canned hams,

00:01:55.123 --> 00:01:56.730
(audience laughing)

00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:59.190
my companion, you know, my wife,

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:00.340
and that's all you need.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:01.950
- And you're not so good at it?

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:03.060
- Well, no, I just,

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.400
I couldn't get anything done.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:08.793
Like, I was just on the
couch watching documentaries.

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:11.070
I was in flannel,

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:12.330
and drinking wine,

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:14.400
crying at documentaries.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.233
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:02:15.233 --> 00:02:16.066
Well, what was your wife doing?

00:02:16.066 --> 00:02:17.521
- She was the butch one.

00:02:17.521 --> 00:02:19.830
(everyone laughing) She was the one,

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:21.240
she was the one that was,

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.550
she spent an entire month outside,

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:24.840
painting our fence,

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:26.904
I think 'cause she got
tired of talking to me.

00:02:26.904 --> 00:02:27.900
(everyone laughing)

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.910
And I was, I was useless.

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:31.104
She like rewired-

00:02:31.104 --> 00:02:32.490
- You didn't, like,
maybe wanna go help her?

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:34.470
- I went one day, I lasted one day,

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:35.303
and I have dainty.

00:02:35.303 --> 00:02:37.770
- I love that you're the one
that points out the one time.

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:39.283
Oh, I was there for one time.

00:02:39.283 --> 00:02:41.310
- I was in the sun for a day.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:42.840
No, I have dainty hands.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.280
That's,
(everyone laughing)

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.020
that's part of what my
special talks about,

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:48.660
is that our roles are reversed

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.970
in a way that you would not think.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.470
- Do you remember that
the first time, like,

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:54.270
the first time you got
paid for doing comedy?

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:55.171
- Oh wow.

00:02:55.171 --> 00:02:56.850
It took a long time to get there.

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:58.347
But yeah, the first time was,

00:02:58.347 --> 00:03:00.660
and I got paid to do an event,

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.730
I think it was in, like, Virginia,

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:05.400
and it was right after I
did "Last Comic Standing"

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:08.160
and whoever hired me had gotten fired,

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:11.137
and the person now in
charge was kinda like,

00:03:11.137 --> 00:03:14.070
"Ah, okay, we'll figure this out"

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:15.240
I got to this venue

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.850
and the stage was a crate,

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:20.160
just a milk crate that you stand on.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:23.100
The light was one of those
construction clamp lights.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.540
- The clip-on? (laughing)
- Yeah.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:25.950
- And the, the sound,

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:29.880
the sound was a very
cheap karaoke machine.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:32.639
And I was like, "Oh, this
is not gonna go well"

00:03:32.639 --> 00:03:35.310
and my opener was
supposed to do 20 minutes.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:36.480
He lasted two minutes,

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.880
because we had this venue that,

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:40.290
it was in a biker bar.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:41.130
It was in a biker bar,

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:43.440
that's not where I was hired to perform,

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.607
and these bikers were
just looking at me going,

00:03:45.607 --> 00:03:47.711
"No. No, thank you"

00:03:47.711 --> 00:03:48.686
(everyone laughing)

00:03:48.686 --> 00:03:49.663
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:03:49.663 --> 00:03:51.240
- I thought it was gonna
be like you won them over,

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:54.498
and suddenly you were dancing
in tandem with the bikers.

00:03:54.498 --> 00:03:56.130
(audience laughing)
- I wish they were just like,

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:59.182
whatever you're talking
about, we don't want.

00:03:59.182 --> 00:04:00.015
(audience laughing)

00:04:00.015 --> 00:04:00.848
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:04:00.848 --> 00:04:03.060
- I had to be up there for 45 minutes.

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:04.570
- Because the other
clown left you hanging?

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:05.403
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:05.403 --> 00:04:07.770
So like, I think I lasted like 30,

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:09.457
and the last 15 I was like,

00:04:09.457 --> 00:04:13.140
"Who wants a Q and A?"
(everyone laughing)

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:15.438
- They were like, "We don't know you"

00:04:15.438 --> 00:04:17.160
(everyone laughing)

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:19.434
- Our question is, who are you.

00:04:19.434 --> 00:04:20.726
(everyone laughing)

00:04:20.726 --> 00:04:21.559
- [Fortune] Yeah.

00:04:21.559 --> 00:04:22.392
- Oh my God.

00:04:22.392 --> 00:04:24.090
Well it, it builds our character.

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:24.923
Those times, yeah.
- It does.

00:04:24.923 --> 00:04:26.280
My mom came with me to that gig.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.690
I was like, first paid gig!

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:30.270
And she was like, "Oh, you..."

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:31.103
- So she's like,

00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:32.242
so this is what you wanna do?

00:04:32.242 --> 00:04:34.263
- Yeah, she's like, "Are
you sure this is it?"

00:04:34.263 --> 00:04:36.600
- Hey, if you lasted there
and you made it through that.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:39.060
- I mean, here we are, 12 years later.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:40.831
I think I'm finally
getting the hang of it.

00:04:40.831 --> 00:04:41.814
- We're with Kelly Clarkson!
- Look at her!

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:43.580
(audience cheering)

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:44.460
- It is funny though,

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:45.963
all of our first jobs, like,

00:04:45.963 --> 00:04:49.020
that you get paid and they're crazy.

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:49.853
Okay.

00:04:49.853 --> 00:04:50.686
Is it true that you also recently

00:04:50.686 --> 00:04:52.620
shot a show with Arnold Schwarzenegger?

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:53.453
- I did, yeah.

00:04:53.453 --> 00:04:54.286
- Wait, what's the show?

00:04:54.286 --> 00:04:57.450
- It's a big action series for Netflix

00:04:57.450 --> 00:04:59.130
coming out sometime next year,

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:00.330
and, uh, yeah, I never-

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:01.530
- Are you doing like action scenes?

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:02.610
- Yeah, I fooled them.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:04.185
See, that's why I wear camo!

00:05:04.185 --> 00:05:05.160
(audience laughing)

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:07.800
I'm fooling people into
thinking I can do action.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.480
But it was, it's so outta my wheelhouse,

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:11.580
but I actually loved it so much.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:14.479
- I hope you're the action
lead and he's the comic foil.

00:05:14.479 --> 00:05:15.600
(everyone laughing)

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:16.433
That's how I want this played.

00:05:16.433 --> 00:05:18.060
- That is the juxtaposition
we're looking for now.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:19.110
- We do laugh a lot,

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:20.550
but it was, it was crazy.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:22.080
I found myself one night,

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:24.540
we were doing this whole action sequence,

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:25.530
and it was just he and I,

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:28.290
and we're like army
crawling across the floor.

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:30.570
There's explosions everywhere.

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:31.927
And he looked at me and he was like,

00:05:31.927 --> 00:05:34.210
"Now you know what I've
been doing for 40 years"

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:35.230
(everyone laughing)

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:36.063
- This is it.

00:05:36.063 --> 00:05:37.838
(Fortune laughing)

00:05:37.838 --> 00:05:38.970
- That's a terrible Arnold impression,

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:40.423
but you guys get it.

00:05:40.423 --> 00:05:41.703
- [Kelly] We all got it.
- [Lena] We felt it.

00:05:42.637 --> 00:05:44.400
"Fortune Feimster: Good Fortune"

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:45.990
premieres on Netflix tomorrow.

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:48.723
You have to watch it if you like laughing.

